0157n  450000100060000000300040000600500170001000800410002704000510006815100270011945100270014645100200017345100400019345100390023394200150027227207DLC20240327170351.0800722n| azannaabn          |a ana        aDLCbengerdacDLCdDLCdWaUdOCoLCdDLCdDNLM  aLeeds (United Kingdom)  aLeeds (West Yorkshire)  aLeeds (England)  aCity and Borough of Leeds (England)  aCity and County of Leeds (England)  aGEOGR_NAME02876nz  a2200289n  450000100060000000300030000600500170000900800410002604000070006711000710007436600270014541000210017250000370019350000410023050000400027150000410031150000390035251000870039152017570047855000710223555000710230655000640237755000590244166700160250090500550251694200150257127208OI20260130160645.0240329|| aca||aabn           | a|a     d  aOI  aMusicExperimentX: Transdisciplinary Encounters in and Beyond Music  k2018/01/01l2020/12/31  aMusicExperimentX  aAssis, Paulo de4Promoter916044  aD'Errico, Lucia4Collaborator919728  aGiudici, Paolo4Collaborator916738  aBotelho, Filipa4Collaborator926646  aStover, Chris4Collaborator927209  aOrpheus Instituut (Ghent, Belgium)1http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q2289519922507  aMusicExperiment X: Transdisciplinary Encounters In and Beyond Music considers performance of Western art music as a privileged locus for the creative problematisation of existing musical objects and entities. Operating beyond conventional modes of music interpretation and representation, this project crucially situates the making of music in a space that transcends music itself, opening wider fields of practice and inquiry. The project aims at renewing musical practices not only through music-specific means, but significantly through non- or extra-musical connections. At the bottom of this approach lies the proposal that musical objects are to be questioned and challenged in depth, and not simply commodified, reproduced, and consumed. Exposing stratified musical entities (such as musical works, musical instruments, practices, or theoretical reflections), in dialogue with other kinds of things and artefacts, this project fosters innovation, aiming at the production of aesthetic and epistemic shiftings. The making of music becomes both a critical and a constructive act: critical in the sense that it renegotiates the boundaries of pre-existing knowledges and practices; constructive in that, through practice, it creates anew its own conditions and materialities.  Operating at the crossroads of performance, composition, and staging, the project explores the design, development, and realization of experimental performances, some of which in collaboration with partner institutions from Belgium, The Netherlands, Norway, and Singapore. In addition to artists and researchers at different levels of experience and expertise (senior, postdoc, and doc researchers), the project also includes doctoral students from the docARTES programme.  aArtistic research1http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q20827087921804  aInterdisciplinarity1http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q849359927077  aPerformance1http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q6942562926223  aOntology1http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q44325924417  aNot present  a24104Principal fundingf1k2018/01/01l2020/12/31  aCORPO_NAME00551nz  a2200169n  450000100060000000300030000600500170000900800410002602400820006704000070014910000180015651000280017494200150020250000660021755000540028355100440033727209OI20260330112324.0240329|| aca||aabn           | a|a     d  1http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1071929889Chris StoveraQ1071929882Wikidata  aOI  aStover, Chris  aMusicExperimentX927208  aPERSO_NAME  aBernard, Jonathan W.917067ihttp://wikidata.org/entity/P1066  aTromboneihttp://wikidata.org/entity/P1303921860  aUSAihttp://wikidata.org/entity/P2794300632nz  a2200205n  4500001000600000003000300006005001700009008004100026024007800067040000700145100003800152400002000190400002200210400001900